+# ION Agent Branch Capsule Bootstrap Binding Protocol v0.1
+
+Status: active provisional protocol
+Created: 2026-05-11
+Authority: Codex terminal startup/context loading only
+Production authority: false
+Live execution authority: false
+
+## Purpose
+
+This protocol makes the Agent Branch Capsule Protocol visible to new Codex
+terminals without directly editing settled shared Capsule, Mini, HOT_CONTEXT, or
+Status surfaces.
+
+The branch-capsule protocol remains settlement-governed. This binding only
+defines how new carrier sessions discover and carry its non-negotiable startup
+law.
+
+## Source protocol
+
+```text
+ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+```
+
+## Boot-loaded law
+
+Every new Codex terminal should be told:
+
+```text
+Shared Codex solo context is read-only base memory.
+Material work requires a unique branch capsule identity.
+Branch outputs are candidate state only.
+Settlement inbox is the only merge path back into shared context.
+Only a settler assigns checkpoint/C-numbers or mutates shared context.
+```
+
+## Boot surfaces
+
+This law is carried by these boot/load surfaces:
+
+```text
+.codex/config.toml
+.codex/hooks/ion_session_start_context.py
+ION/04_packages/kernel/ion_codex_solo_context.py
+ION/05_context/current/codex_solo/CONTEXT_PACKAGES.json
+ION/05_context/current/codex_solo/ROUTE.json
+ION/03_registry/ion_skill_registry.yaml
+```
+
+## Required default context package
+
+New Codex sessions should include:
+
+```text
+agent_branch_capsule_bootstrap_package
+```
+
+The package should reference:
+
+```text
+ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+ION/02_architecture/ION_AGENT_BRANCH_CAPSULE_BOOTSTRAP_BINDING_PROTOCOL_V0_1.md
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/BRANCH_CAPSULE_REGISTRY_V0_1.json
+ION/05_context/current/context_settlement/CONTEXT_SETTLEMENT_REGISTRY_V0_1.json
+ION/04_packages/kernel/ion_agent_branch_capsule.py
+```
+
+## Hook behavior
+
+The SessionStart hook remains read-only. It should not create a branch by
+itself. It should inject a short branch-capsule law block and the route paths a
+worker must use to create or validate a branch before material work.
+
+## Canon boundary
+
+This protocol does not by itself settle the branch-capsule protocol into shared
+checkpoint canon. It creates a candidate bootstrap binding so new terminals see
+the law reliably while the context settler reviews promotion.
+
+## Non-claims
+
+This protocol does not:
+
+```text
+edit CAPSULE.md
+edit MINI.md
+edit HOT_CONTEXT.md
+edit STATUS.json
+assign a C-number
+settle candidate branch work
+grant production authority
+grant live execution authority
+create active branches automatically
+```
+
+## Next implementation lane
+
+After settlement, implement:
+
+```text
+branch capsule auto-preflight in queue runner
+active branch visibility in cockpit/drawer
+branch write-scope conflict preflight for task starts
+context settler promotion receipts for accepted branch packets
+```
